  "v85.qcd.title": "Where does proton mass come from?",
  "v85.qcd.intro": "Three quarks are a useful shorthand, not a complete description. This optional article connects particle physics with the meaning of mass, without adding a solver.",
  "v85.qcd.valence.title": "1 · More than three little spheres",
  "v85.qcd.valence.text": "“Two up, one down” describes the valence excess: two more up quarks than up antiquarks, and one more down quark than down antiquarks. The proton contains dynamical quark, antiquark and gluon fields. Three stationary spheres on fixed orbits do not describe this quantum state.",
